  "notes": "A magazine-style show script: after tonight's six matches, a \"Christmas Chaos Update\" segment previews the fed's Christmas Day 1996 pay-per-view (two survival-style elimination matches -- Power Team USA vs. an Amish Warrior-led trio, and the Thunderdome Warriors vs. the Golden Alliance -- plus a sealed steel-cage match for the vacant IWF Television Championship, Flawed to Perfection vs. Butterball), and the broadcast closes previewing that Sunday's IWF Sunday Night's Main Event card, including IWF United States and Universal Tag Team title defenses and a quarterfinal round of an IWF 3-man tag team tournament -- none of which the held record's single surviving document shows contested."
